---
/**
 * Decorative scroll cue: rotating "SCROLL DOWN" ring with a centre arrow.
 * Colours come from `currentColor`, so it inherits whatever text token the
 * parent sets instead of hardcoding the dark hex.
 *
 * The ring and the arrow are two separate `<svg>` boxes on purpose.
 *
 * The obvious build — one SVG whose `<text>`/`<textPath>` carries the rotation —
 * costs a document-wide layout on *every* animation frame. An SVG `transform`
 * is applied by Blink during SVG layout, not by the compositor, so the animated
 * text invalidates layout up the whole ancestor chain, and on this page that
 * chain ends at the document: the browser is then re-laying-out a 3 000 px
 * page 60 times a second while the reader scrolls. Measured with CDP
 * `Performance.getMetrics`: 24 layouts during a five-step scroll on the home
 * page versus 0 on `/works` and `/profile`; `display: none` on this component
 * drops it back to 0, which is what identified it.
 *
 * Rotating the `<svg>` element itself is a transform on an HTML box, so it is
 * composited (`will-change: transform`) and never touches layout. The arrow is
 * a sibling, so it stays upright.
 */
---

<div class="circle-container text-dark" aria-hidden="true">
	<svg class="cue-ring" viewBox="0 0 100 100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
		<defs>
			<path
				id="circlePath"
				d="M 50, 50 m -37, 0 a 37,37 0 1,1 74,0 a 37,37 0 1,1 -74,0"
				fill="transparent"
			></path>
		</defs>

		<text>
			<textPath href="#circlePath"> • SCROLL DOWN • SCROLL DOWN </textPath>
		</text>
	</svg>

	<svg class="cue-arrow" viewBox="0 0 100 100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
		<polygon points="42,45 58,45 50,57"></polygon>
	</svg>
</div>

<style>
	.circle-container {
		width: 80px;
		height: 80px;
		position: relative;
	}

	/* Both layers fill the same box; only the ring spins. */
	.cue-ring,
	.cue-arrow {
		position: absolute;
		inset: 0;
		width: 100%;
		height: 100%;
	}

	.cue-ring {
		transform-origin: 50% 50%;
		/* Own compositor layer: rotating it never re-runs layout or repaint. */
		will-change: transform;
		animation: rotateRing 20s linear infinite;
	}

	text {
		font-size: 10px;
		font-weight: bold;
		letter-spacing: 2px;
		fill: currentColor;
	}

	/* Centre arrow */
	.cue-arrow {
		fill: currentColor;
	}

	@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
		.cue-ring {
			animation: none;
			will-change: auto;
		}
	}

	@keyframes rotateRing {
		from {
			transform: rotate(0deg);
		}
		to {
			transform: rotate(360deg);
		}
	}
</style>
